Refuse a context with an n_ubatch that is not larger than n_rs_seq + 1
Fold-into: upstream/llama-context

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- A context with n_ubatch <= n_rs_seq + 1 stops the process at its first decode.

  The recurrent memory keeps the last n_rs_seq + 1 tokens of each sequence in one ubatch, and
  llama_batch_allocr::split_equal asserts n_ubatch > n_rs_seq + 1. llama_init_from_model accepts a
  smaller n_ubatch, and the first decode of a recurrent or hybrid model then stops the process on
  GGML_ASSERT(n_ubatch > n_keep_tail).

  The change: The context constructor throws std::runtime_error for such parameters, thus
  llama_init_from_model returns nullptr with an error line.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--ubatch-tail.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
    src/llama-context.cpp
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -246,6 +246,15 @@ llama_context::llama_context(
 
     cparams.n_ubatch = std::min(cparams.n_batch, params.n_ubatch == 0 ? params.n_batch : params.n_ubatch);
 
+    // [TAG_RECURRENT_ROLLBACK_SPLITS] the recurrent memory keeps the last n_rs_seq + 1 tokens of
+    // each sequence in one ubatch, and llama_batch_allocr::split_equal asserts
+    // n_ubatch > n_rs_seq + 1 on each decode. Refuse such a context here, with an error that the
+    // caller gets, and not with an abort at the first decode.
+    if (cparams.n_rs_seq > 0 && cparams.n_ubatch <= cparams.n_rs_seq + 1) {
+        throw std::runtime_error("n_ubatch (" + std::to_string(cparams.n_ubatch) + ") must be larger than n_rs_seq + 1 (" +
+                                 std::to_string(cparams.n_rs_seq + 1) + "): the last n_rs_seq + 1 tokens of a sequence stay in one ubatch");
+    }
+
     cparams.n_outputs_max = params.n_outputs_max == 0 || llama_model_has_encoder(&model) ? cparams.n_batch : params.n_outputs_max;
     cparams.n_outputs_max_per_seq = params.n_outputs_max_per_seq == 0 ?
             cparams.n_outputs_max : std::min(params.n_outputs_max_per_seq, cparams.n_outputs_max);
